      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "To compare the effect of transcervical resection of the endometrium (TCRE) combined with levonorgestrel-containing intrauterine system (LNG-IUS) versus LNG-IUS alone in the treatment of adenomyosis."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "STUDY DESIGN",
          "content": "A total of 43 patients with adenomyosis, suffering from dysmenorrhea and menorrhagia, were recruited. Twenty patients underwent TCRE first followed by insertion of the LNG-IUS (group 1), while 23 patients were managed with the LNG-IUS alone (group 2). Both groups were followed up at 3, 6 and 12 months with regard to menstrual characteristics. Visual analogue scores, transvaginal ultrasound scans and routine gynecological examinations were performed on all patients during the follow-up visits."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "There was a significant reduction in menstrual flow and pain in both groups following treatment. The reduction in menstrual flow in group 1 was significantly (p < 0.001) greater than that of group 2 at 3, 6 and 12 months posttreatment. On the other hand, there was no significant difference (p = 0.061) in the reduction of pain between the two groups."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "TCRE combined with LNG-IUS for the treatment ofadenomyosis is more effective in reducing menstrual flow compared with the LNG-IUS alone. However, there was no demonstrable difference in the amount of pain reduction between the two treatment strategies."
        }
      ]},
